  "transcript": "Stand behind the counter for a second. Look at the store's side. A product sells for $10. It costs the store $4 to make. 50% off, you pay five. The store spent four to make it. So five minus four. The store keeps $1. I one, get one free, you pay 10 and take two, but those two cost the store eight to make. So 10 minus eight, the store keeps $2. Double. So it is the same $5 an item for you, but double the profit for the store. And the sign never changed. It still says 10. You paid full price and felt clever doing it. Oh, and this trick is old. A pottery guy named Wedgewood ran it back in the 1700s. So no, you are not the first sucker. You are just the latest.",
